<script>
import { url } from '@abide/abide'

import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import DealSearch from './lib/DealSearch.abide'
import dealSearch from './lib/DealSearch.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import StageEntries from './lib/StageEntries.abide'
import stageEntries from './lib/StageEntries.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/reactive/derived',
        '/reactive/reactive',
        '/reactive/refresh',
        '/handlers/get',
        '/ambients/abort-signal',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/reactive.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('reactive.derived is unkeyed and memo keyed, whatever the body declares — 11.1, 11.2, 11.3'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/reactive.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('memo refuses anything but a body at construction — 11.73'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/memoOptions.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a memo gates and shapes what its function settles to — 11.79'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Keep one entry per stage">
        <p>A <code>memo</code> holds one entry per set of args, each held and reloaded on its own,
            so going back to a stage shows its count without loading it again. Read an entry by
            calling the <code>memo</code> inside a <code>reactive.derived</code>, which follows the
            stage as it changes.</p>
        <Example code={stageEntries}><StageEntries /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Search once the typing stops, on this page alone">
        <p>Where the handler declares no pace, or one this page does not want, read it through a
            <code>memo</code> with a <code>debounce</code>, and a new query is searched once the
            typing pauses rather than once per keystroke. A pace every page should keep goes on the
            <a href={url('/handlers/get')}><code>GET</code></a> itself.</p>
        <Example code={dealSearch}><DealSearch /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Look again five minutes after the last look, while the panel is open">
        <p>Give the <code>memo</code> a <code>ttl</code>. An entry a page reads is looked at again
            that long after its last answer landed, and the old answer stays up meanwhile; one
            nothing reads is let go, and the next read looks afresh. Work that has to run whether or
            not anything reads it is a <a href={url('/orchestration/job')}><code>job</code></a>
            writing the memo.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="shared" code={`
            import { memo } from '@abide/abide'
            import { DEALS } from '../../pipeline/lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export const followUps = memo(
                async function* () {
                    for (const deal of DEALS)
                        if (deal.stage === 'lead') yield deal.name
                },
                { global: true, tags: ['follow-ups'], ttl: 300_000 },
            )
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Keep only the headcount from each registry entry">
        <p>Give the <code>memo</code> a <code>transform</code>, and each entry keeps what it hands
            back, so a call answers the headcount rather than the whole record. A
            <code>schema</code> checks what the function settles to before that, and an
            <code>identity</code> says when a new value is the same one, as they do on a
            <a href={url('/reactive/reactive')}><code>reactive</code></a>.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { fetchAndHandle, memo } from '@abide/abide'
            import { registryOrigin } from './registryOrigin.server.ts'

            type Registration = { founded: number; employees: number }

            export const headcounts = memo(
                ({ id }: { id: string }) =>
                    fetchAndHandle<Registration>(\`\${registryOrigin()}/companies/\${id}\`),
                { global: true, transform: (entry) => entry.employees },
            )
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
